	<Section num="04" label="Startup" title="One host project, one startup call." alt lede="All three extensions resolve the same host project, found by its host key rather than its display name. Register them before the chain ends, migrate Beacon's schema, then sync.">
		<Flow
			seconds={7}
			steps={[
				{ label: 'Register', detail: 'ExposeDbContext and ExposeDocs on the Beacon builder.' },
				{ label: 'End the chain', detail: 'UseSqlServer or UsePostgreSql last: it returns IServiceCollection.' },
				{ label: 'Add tools', detail: 'AddBeaconMcp().AddHostEndpointTools for the same project.' },
				{ label: 'Migrate', detail: 'UseBeacon creates the schema and applies migrations.' },
				{ label: 'Sync', detail: 'SyncBeaconHostAsync: data sources first, then documents.', tone: 'ok' },
				{ label: 'Serve', detail: 'Endpoint tools appear once the host project exists.' },
			]}
		/>
		<div class="cols2 startup">
			<Code code={STARTUP} lang="csharp" title="Program.cs" />
			<div class="stack">
				<div class="card mini">
					<h3>Idempotent</h3>
					<p>The first run creates the project, the data source and the link. Later runs rewrite metadata only when the hash of the exposed model slice changed, and re-chunk only the documents that changed.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card mini">
					<h3>Safe on several replicas</h3>
					<p>The sync holds one lock in Beacon's database (<code>pg_try_advisory_lock</code> on PostgreSQL, <code>sp_getapplock</code> on SQL Server). Replicas starting together run it one after another, waiting up to 5 minutes.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card mini">
					<h3>Found by its host key</h3>
					<p>The host project carries <code>host:shop</code>. A user project already named "Shop" is left untouched, and the host project is created as "Shop (host)".</p>
				</div>
				<p class="note"><code>SyncBeaconHostDataSourcesAsync()</code> syncs the data sources only, for hosts that do not ship documents.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</Section>

